# Data Agent MCP Server environment example — public placeholders only.
# Security-remediation implementation is under validation; release gates remain open.
# Loaded from $DATA_AGENT_ENV_FILE, else ./.env, without overriding process env.
# Prefer managed environment injection for secrets and the SDK default chain.
# Actual secret-bearing .env (including dotenv loaded at startup), YAML and JSON
# must be process-owned regular files in trusted directories, POSIX 0600/0400.
# Public placeholder-only examples may be 0644; this is not a secret-file exemption.
# No automatic chmod/chown/migration. Obtain admin authorization for real changes.
# Projected/symlink secrets and Windows ACLs require supported validation; otherwise
# use managed environment injection, not permission-check bypasses. See README.md.

# Optional explicit credentials for the credentials-go default chain.
# Leave these commented/absent for an instance/workload-role or other SDK provider.
# The base principal needs sts:AssumeRole on mapped roles; roles must trust it.
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<access-key-id>
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=<access-key-secret>
# Required with AK/SK for temporary credentials:
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_SECURITY_TOKEN=<sts-security-token>
# Static STS env values do not self-renew. Retain a refreshable SDK provider for
# long-running deployments. CLI profiles are not automatically imported.
# Removed API Key inputs are rejected even with the gateway off; see README.md.

# Optional overrides (highest priority, above config.yaml).
#DATA_AGENT_REGION=cn-hangzhou
#DATA_AGENT_DMS_UNIT=
#DATA_AGENT_DMS_ENTERPRISE_ENDPOINT=
#DATA_AGENT_ENDPOINT=
#DATA_AGENT_WORKSPACE_ID=
#DATA_AGENT_CUSTOM_AGENT_ID=
#DATA_AGENT_SESSIONS_DIR=
#DATA_AGENT_CONFIG=./config.yaml

# ALL remote HTTP/SSE deployments require YAML identity.enabled=true,
# require_identity=true, a valid identity.namespace and this nonempty token.
# Applies with gateway on/off to initialize, tools/list, tools/call, notifications
# and every GET/POST/DELETE. No legacy/header/global-identity fallback.
# Header mode: token only for trusted proxies that overwrite client identity.
#IDENTITY_AUTH_TOKEN=<platform-auth-token>
# Legacy aliases: AILY_SHARED_SECRET / IDENTITY_SHARED_SECRET.

# JWT mode requires a valid HS256 token with exp, tenant_id, agent_id and user_id
# or email on every request, not only gateway calls. JWT groups/default need
# exact tenant/agent scopes in YAML; header-mode mappings must leave scopes empty.
#IDENTITY_JWT_SECRET=<jwt-signing-key>
# HMAC keys are used as-is, not base64-decoded. Additional keys have EQUIVALENT
# signing authority in ONE trusted domain (rotation or mutually trusted apps).
# Never combine untrusted organizations/issuers; use separate instances/roots.
#IDENTITY_JWT_SECRETS=<additional-trusted-key>,<rotation-key>

# agent_gateway has no additional gateway token. P2b remains off by default.
# HTTP limits and identity.max_tenants (128 cached + initializing total) use YAML;
# explicit zero/negative limits reject startup, rather than disabling protection.
# dacli's AILY_TOKEN / AILY_JWT are CLIENT credentials, not server signing secrets;
# provision them separately. dacli remains a Streamable HTTP client, not SSE.
